"A new cmake option, `BUILD_OFFLOAD_COMPRESS`. When rocPRIM is build with "
"this option enabled, the `--offload-compress` switch is passed to the "
"compiler. This causes the compiler to compress the binary that it "
"generates. Compression can be useful in cases where you are compiling for"
" a large number of targets, since this often results in a large binary. "
"Without compression, in some cases, the generated binary may become so "
"large symbols are placed out of range, resulting in linking errors. The "
"new `BUILD_OFFLOAD_COMPRESS` option is set to `ON` by default."
