"`rocprim::arch::wavefront::max_size()` for compile-time constants. Use "
"these when allocating global or shared memory. For run-time constants, "
"use `rocprim::arch::wavefront::size()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:3699
msgid ""
"The default scan accumulator types for device-level scan algorithms will "
"be changed in an upcoming release, resulting in a breaking change. "
"Previously, the default accumulator type was set to the input type for "
"the inclusive scans and to the initial value type for the exclusive "
"scans. This could lead to unexpected overflow if the input or initial "
"type was smaller than the output type when the accumulator type wasn't "
"explicitly set using the `AccType` template parameter. The new default "
"accumulator types will be set to the type that results when the input or "
"initial value type is applied to the scan operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:3701
msgid ""
"The following is the complete list of affected functions and how their "
"default accumulator types are changing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:3704 ../../release/changelog.md:3707
msgid ""
"current default: `class AccType = typename "
"std::iterator_traits<InputIterator>::value_type>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:3705 ../../release/changelog.md:3708
msgid ""
"future default: `class AccType = "
"rocprim::invoke_result_binary_op_t<typename "
"std::iterator_traits<InputIterator>::value_type, BinaryFunction>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:3710 ../../release/changelog.md:3713
msgid "current default: `class AccType = detail::input_type_t<InitValueType>>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:3711 ../../release/changelog.md:3714
msgid ""
"future default: `class AccType = "
"rocprim::invoke_result_binary_op_t<rocprim::detail::input_type_t<InitValueType>,"
" BinaryFunction>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:3716
