" CPU metrics and telemetry through the AMD SMI API and CLI tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8078
msgid ""
"New architecture support. CK now supports to the following architectures "
"to enable efficient image denoising on the following AMD GPUs: gfx1030, "
"gfx1100, gfx1031, gfx1101, gfx1032, gfx1102, gfx1034, gfx1103, gfx1035, "
"gfx1036"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8085
msgid ""
"FP8 rounding logic is replaced with stochastic rounding. Stochastic "
"rounding mimics a more realistic data behavior and improves model "
"convergence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8088
msgid "**HIP** (6.1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8092
msgid ""
"New environment variable to enable kernel run serialization. The default "
"`HIP_LAUNCH_BLOCKING` value is `0` (disable); which causes kernels to run"
" as defined in the queue. When set to `1` (enable), the HIP runtime "
"serializes the kernel queue, which behaves the same as "
"`AMD_SERIALIZE_KERNEL`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8101
msgid ""
"New GemmTuning extension parameter. GemmTuning allows you to set a "
"split-k value for each solution, which is more feasible for performance "
"tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8104
msgid "**hipFFT** (1.0.14)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8108
msgid ""
"New multi-GPU support for single-process transforms. Multiple GPUs can be"
" used to perform a transform in a single process. Note that this initial "
"implementation is a functional preview."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8111 ../../release/changelog.md:8312
msgid "**HIPIFY** (17.0.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8115
msgid ""
"Skipped code blocks: Code blocks that are skipped by the preprocessor are"
" no longer hipified under the `--default-preprocessor` option. To hipify "
"everything, despite conditional preprocessor directives (`#if`, `#ifdef`,"
" `#ifndef`, `#elif`, or `#else`), don't use the `--default-preprocessor` "
"or `--amap` options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8119
msgid "**hipSPARSELt** (0.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8123
msgid ""
"Structured sparsity matrix support extensions. Structured sparsity "
"matrices help speed up deep-learning workloads. We now support `B` as the"
" sparse matrix and `A` as the dense matrix in Sparse Matrix-Matrix "
"Multiplication (SPMM). Prior to this release, we only supported sparse "
"(matrix A) x dense (matrix B) matrix multiplication. Structured sparsity "
"matrices help speed up deep learning workloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8129
msgid "**hipTensor** (1.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8133
msgid ""
"4D tensor permutation and contraction support. You can now perform tensor"
" permutation on 4D tensors and 4D contractions for F16, BF16, and Complex"
" F32/F64 datatypes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8137 ../../release/changelog.md:8347
msgid "**llvm-project** (17.0.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8141
msgid ""
"Combined projects. ROCm Device-Libs, ROCm Compiler Support, and hipCC are"
" now located in the `llvm-project/amd` subdirectory of AMD's fork of the "
"LLVM project. Previously, these projects were maintained in separate "
"repositories. Note that the projects themselves will continue to be "
"packaged separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8146
msgid ""
"Split the `rocm-llvm` package. This package has been split into a "
"required and an optional package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8148
msgid ""
"**rocm-llvm(required)**: A package containing the essential binaries "
"needed for compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8150
msgid ""
"**rocm-llvm-dev(optional)**: A package containing binaries for compiler "
"and application developers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8152
msgid "**MIGraphX** (2.9.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8156
msgid ""
"Improved performance for transformer-based models. We added support for "
"FlashAttention, which benefits models like BERT, GPT, and Stable "
"Diffusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8159
msgid ""
"New Torch-MIGraphX driver. This driver calls MIGraphX directly from "
"PyTorch. It provides an `mgx_module` object that you can invoke like any "
"other Torch module, but which utilizes the MIGraphX inference engine "
"internally. Torch-MIGraphX supports FP32, FP16, and INT8 datatypes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8164
msgid ""
"FP8 support. We now offer functional support for inference in the "
"FP8E4M3FNUZ datatype. You can load an ONNX model in FP8E4M3FNUZ using C++"
" or Python APIs, or `migraphx-driver`. You can quantize a floating point "
"model to FP8 format by using the `--fp8` flag with `migraphx-driver`. To "
"accelerate inference, MIGraphX uses hardware acceleration on MI300 for "
"FP8 by leveraging FP8 support in various backend kernel libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8170
msgid "**MIOpen** (3.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8174
msgid ""
"Improved performance for inference and convolutions. Inference support "
"now provided for Find 2.0 fusion plans. Additionally, we've enhanced the "
"Number of samples, Height, Width, and Channels (NHWC) convolution kernels"
" for heuristics. NHWC stores data in a format where the height and width "
"dimensions come first, followed by channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8179
msgid "**OpenMP** (17.60.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8183
msgid ""
"New MI300 FP atomics. Application performance can now improve by "
"leveraging fast floating-point atomics on MI300 (gfx942)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8187
msgid ""
"Implicit Zero-copy is triggered automatically in XNACK-enabled MI300A "
"systems. Implicit Zero-copy behavior in `non unified_shared_memory` "
"programs is triggered automatically in XNACK-enabled MI300A systems (for "
"example, when using the `HSA_XNACK=1` environment variable). OpenMP "
"supports the 'requires `unified_shared_memory`' directive to support "
"programs that don’t want to copy data explicitly between the CPU and GPU."
" However, this requires that you add these directives to every "
"translation unit of the program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8198
msgid ""
"NCCL 2.18.6 compatibility. RCCL is now compatible with NCCL 2.18.6, which"
" includes increasing the maximum IB network interfaces to 32 and fixing "
"network device ordering when creating communicators with only one GPU per"
" node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8202
msgid ""
"Doubled simultaneous communication channels. We improved MI300X "
"performance by increasing the maximum number of simultaneous "
"communication channels from 32 to 64."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8206
msgid "**rocALUTION** (3.1.1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8210
msgid ""
"New multiple node and GPU support. Unsmoothed and smoothed aggregations "
"and Ruge-Stueben AMG now work with multiple nodes and GPUs. For more "
"information, refer to the  [API "
"documentation](https://rocm.docs.amd.com/projects/rocALUTION/en/docs-6.1.0/usermanual/solvers.html"
"#unsmoothed-aggregation-amg)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8215
msgid "**rocDecode** (0.5.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8219
msgid ""
"New ROCm component. rocDecode ROCm's newest component, providing high-"
"performance video decode support for AMD GPUs. To learn more, refer to "
"the  "
"[documentation](https://rocm.docs.amd.com/projects/rocDecode/en/latest/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8228
msgid ""
"C++ upgrades. RDC was upgraded from C++11 to C++17 to enable a more "
"modern C++ standard when writing RDC plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8231
msgid "**RPP** (1.5.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8235
msgid ""
"New backend support. Audio processing support added for the `HOST` "
"backend and 3D Voxel kernels support for the `HOST` and `HIP` backends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8239 ../../release/changelog.md:8411
msgid "**ROCm Validation Suite** (1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8243
msgid ""
"New datatype support. Added BF16 and FP8 datatypes based on General "
"Matrix Multiply(GEMM) operations in the GPU Stress Test (GST) module. "
"This provides additional performance benchmarking and stress testing "
"based on the newly supported datatypes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8246
msgid "**rocSOLVER** (3.25.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8250
msgid ""
"New EigenSolver routine. Based on the Jacobi algorithm, a new EigenSolver"
" routine was added to the library. This routine computes the eigenvalues "
"and eigenvectors of a matrix with improved performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8253
msgid "**ROCTracer** (4.1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8257
msgid ""
"New versioning and callback enhancements. Improved to match versioning "
"changes in HIP Runtime and supports runtime API callbacks and activity "
"record logging. The APIs of different runtimes at different levels are "
"considered different API domains with assigned domain IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8260
msgid "ROCm 6.0.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8262
msgid ""
"See the [ROCm 6.0.2 release "
"notes](https://rocm.docs.amd.com/en/docs-6.0.2/about/release-notes.html) "
"for a complete overview of this release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8265
msgid "**hipFFT** (1.0.13)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8269
msgid ""
"Removed the Git submodule for shared files between rocFFT and hipFFT; "
"instead, just copy the files over (this should help simplify downstream "
"builds and packaging)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8272
msgid "ROCm 6.0.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8274
msgid ""
"See the [ROCm 6.0.0 release "
"notes](https://rocm.docs.amd.com/en/docs-6.0.0/about/release-notes.html) "
"for a complete overview of this release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8277
msgid "**AMD SMI** (23.4.2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8281
msgid ""
"Integrated the E-SMI (EPYC-SMI) library. You can now query CPU-related "
"information directly through AMD SMI. Metrics include power, energy, "
"performance, and other system details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8285
msgid ""
"Added support for gfx942 metrics. You can now query MI300 device metrics "
"to get real-time information. Metrics include power, temperature, energy,"
" and performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8289
msgid "**HIP** (6.0.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8293
msgid "New features to improve resource interoperability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8294
msgid "For external resource interoperability, we've added new structs and enums."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8295
msgid ""
"We've added new members to HIP struct `hipDeviceProp_t` for surfaces, "
"textures, and device identifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8300
msgid ""
"Changes impacting backward compatibility. There are several changes "
"impacting backward compatibility: we changed some struct members and some"
" enum values, and removed some deprecated flags. For additional "
"information, please refer to the Changelog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8305
msgid "**hipCUB** (3.0.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8309
msgid ""
"Additional CUB API support. The hipCUB backend is updated to CUB and "
"Thrust 2.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8316
msgid ""
"Hipified rocSPARSE. We've implemented support for the direct hipification"
" of additional cuSPARSE APIs into rocSPARSE APIs under the `--roc` "
"option. This covers a major milestone in the roadmap towards complete "
"cuSPARSE-to-rocSPARSE hipification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8323
msgid ""
"Enhanced CUDA2HIP document generation. API versions are now listed in the"
" CUDA2HIP documentation. To see if the application binary interface (ABI)"
" has changed, refer to the [*C* "
"column](https://rocm.docs.amd.com/projects/HIPIFY/en/latest/tables/CUDA_Runtime_API_functions_supported_by_HIP.html)"
" in our API documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8329
msgid "**hipRAND** (2.10.16)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8331
msgid ""
"Official release. hipRAND is now a *standalone project*--it's no longer "
"available as a submodule for rocRAND."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8334
msgid "**hipTensor** (1.1.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8338
msgid ""
"Added architecture support. We've added contraction support for gfx942 "
"architectures, and f32 and f64 data types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8344
msgid ""
"Upgraded testing infrastructure. hipTensor will now support dynamic "
"parameter configuration with input YAML config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8351
msgid ""
"Added kernel argument optimization on gfx942. With the new feature, you "
"can preload kernel arguments into Scalar General-Purpose Registers "
"(SGPRs) rather than pass them in memory. This feature is enabled with a "
"compiler option, which also controls the number of arguments to pass in "
"SGPRs. For more information, see: [https://llvm.org/docs/AMDGPUUsage.html"
"#preloaded-kernel-arguments](https://llvm.org/docs/AMDGPUUsage.html"
"#preloaded-kernel-arguments)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8359
msgid ""
"Improved register allocation at -O0. We've improved the register "
"allocator used at -O0 to avoid compiler crashes (when the signature is "
"'ran out of registers during register allocation')."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8363
msgid ""
"Improved generation of debug information. We've improved compile time "
"when generating debug information for certain corner cases. We've also "
"improved the compiler to eliminate compiler crashes when generating debug"
" information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8367
msgid "**MIGraphX** (2.8.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8371
msgid ""
"Added TorchMIGraphX. We introduced a Dynamo backend for Torch, which "
"allows PyTorch to use MIGraphX directly without first requiring a model "
"to be converted to the ONNX model format. With a single line of code, "
"PyTorch users can utilize the performance and quantization benefits "
"provided by MIGraphX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8376
msgid ""
"Added INT8 support across the MIGraphX portfolio. We now support the INT8"
" data type. MIGraphX can perform the quantization or ingest prequantized "
"models. INT8 support extends to the MIGraphX execution provider for ONNX "
"Runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8380
msgid ""
"Boosted overall performance with rocMLIR. We've integrated the rocMLIR "
"library for ROCm-supported RDNA and CDNA GPUs. This technology provides "
"MLIR-based convolution and GEMM kernel generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8384
msgid "**ROCgdb** (13.2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8388
msgid "Added support for additional GPU architectures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8389
msgid "Navi 3 Series: gfx1100, gfx1101, and gfx1102."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8390
msgid "MI300 Series: gfx942."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8392
msgid "**ROCm SMI** (6.0.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8396
msgid ""
"Improved accessibility to GPU partition nodes. You can now view, set, and"
" reset the compute and memory partitions. You'll also get notifications "
"of a GPU busy state, which helps you avoid partition set or reset "
"failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8402
msgid ""
"Upgraded GPU metrics version 1.4. The upgraded GPU metrics binary has an "
"improved metric version format with a content version appended to it. You"
" can read each metric within the binary without the full "
"`rsmi_gpu_metric_t` data structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8407
msgid ""
"Updated GPU index sorting. We made GPU index sorting consistent with "
"other ROCm software tools by optimizing it to use `Bus:Device.Function` "
"(BDF) instead of the card number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8415
msgid ""
"Added GPU and operating system support. We added support for MI300X GPU "
"in GPU Stress Test (GST)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8418
msgid "**ROCProfiler** (2.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8422
msgid ""
"Added option to specify desired ROCProfiler version. You can now use "
"rocProfV1 or rocProfV2 by specifying your desired version, as the legacy "
"rocProf (`rocprofv1`) provides the option to use the latest version "
"(`rocprofv2`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8426
msgid ""
"Added ATT support for parallel kernels. The automatic ISA dumping process"
" also helps ATT successfully parse multiple kernels running in parallel, "
"and provide cycle-accurate occupancy information for multiple kernels at "
"the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8432
msgid ""
"Automated the ISA dumping process by Advance Thread Tracer. Advance "
"Thread Tracer (ATT) no longer depends on user-supplied Instruction Set "
"Architecture (ISA) and compilation process (using ``hipcc --save-temps``)"
" to dump ISA from the running kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8436
msgid "**ROCr Runtime** (1.12.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8440
msgid ""
"Support for SDMA link aggregation. If multiple XGMI links are available "
"when making SDMA copies between GPUs, the copy is distributed over "
"multiple links to increase peak bandwidth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8444
msgid "**rocThrust** (3.0.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8448
msgid ""
"Added Thrust 2.1 API support. rocThrust backend is updated to Thrust and "
"CUB 2.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8451
msgid "**rocWMMA** (1.3.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8455
msgid ""
"**Added new architecture support**.   We added support for gfx942 "
"architectures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8458
msgid ""
"**Added data type support**.   We added support for f8, bf8, xf32 data "
"types on supporting architectures, and for bf16 in the HIP RTC   "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8462
msgid ""
"**Added support for the PyTorch kernel plugin**.   We added awareness of "
"`__HIP_NO_HALF_CONVERSIONS__` to support PyTorch users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8465
msgid "**TransferBench** (beta)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8469
msgid ""
"Improved ordering control. You can now set the thread block size "
"(`BLOCK_SIZE`) and the thread block order (`BLOCK_ORDER`) in which thread"
" blocks from different transfers are run when using a single stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8473
msgid ""
"Added comprehensive reports. We modified individual transfers to report X"
" Compute Clusters (XCC) ID when `SHOW_ITERATIONS` is set to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../release/changelog.md:8477
msgid ""
"Improved accuracy in result validation. You can now validate results for "
"each iteration instead of just once for all iterations."
msgstr ""

